<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre de La Baume</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1477–1544</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre de La Baume was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> from 1522 and the last bishop to reside in the city. Caught between the Duke of Savoy and the citizens, who allied with Fribourg and Bern, he left Geneva in 1533, and the city adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in 1536. He later became archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besancon">Besançon</a> and a cardinal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-de-la-baume.jpg" alt="Pierre de La Baume" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_de_La_Baume.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
